      "id": 1,
      "text": "Lake City was laid out in 1914 and named for the many lakes found throughout the surrounding area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_City%2C_South_Dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Lake City is situated in the Glacial Lakes and Prairies region, which is characterized by numerous lakes formed by glacial activity.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/lake_city_south_dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early settlers began claiming land around Lake City in the 1880s, drawn by the fertile glacial soils and proximity to water.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/lake_city_south_dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The arrival of the railroad prompted local residents to vote for separation from Eden Township to incorporate Lake City as an independent municipality.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/lake_city_south_dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Mechanization in the late 20th century reduced the need for local labor, impacting Lake City's status as an agricultural outpost.",
